Agent: schedulerSession owns teardown: stopActiveSources fences sources at an audio instant with a 5 ms ramp (cutSourceAt). That will matter for the second bug.

Now the doubled audio. When an edit changes which content a part plays (comp swipe, take swap, move, trim, delete, mute) during playback, nothing stops the source already emitted for the old content. The next pass schedules the new part, and both sound.

Simplest option: on any arrangement store change during playback, stop every active audio source and reschedule from the playhead. One flush, guaranteed consistent.

José: fine, flush. simplest thing that's obviously correct. do the stall part first though.

