Agent: First cut: a small table from quality words to forbidden operations. "intimate" → no reverb, no delay. "low end" → no EQ below 200 Hz, no sub-bass device. When the preview comes back, if the batch contains a forbidden operation, reject the card with "violates: keep the vocal intimate".

José: two problems. one, rejecting after preview means the user sees a card that can't be confirmed, and the planner never learns why. if a proposal edits what the clause excludes, send it back to the planner as a correctable rejection with the clause named, so it proposes something else. two, "no reverb" isn't the constraint. "intimate" also means the vocal level and dynamics don't move much. so the clause is an excluded edit dimension AND hold goals on measured metrics with a tolerance.

