Agent: How to test:
1. Arm a MIDI track, set a loop from bar 3 to bar 4, start recording a bar before the loop, play a note in that lead-in bar and a different note inside the loop, let it wrap once and stop.
2. Comp the first pass over the whole clip and play it: the lead-in note sounds.
3. Split the clip inside the loop and play again: both notes still sound on the same beats. Undo the split: nothing changes audibly.
4. Comp only the lead-in half of the clip, split inside that half and play: the lead-in note still sounds.
5. Turn on the clip's loop, start a comp region half-way into the pass and play several loop cycles, then split the clip on a loop boundary and play again: each cycle sounds the same as before the split.
6. Give a note in the take a 50% chance, play a few cycles, split on a loop boundary and play again: the note sounds on the same cycles as before.
7. Draw a note just before the loop start, comp over it, then Delete Time across that note and play several cycles: the deleted note never comes back.
8. Export the arrangement: the render matches what you heard.

