Agent: Every alternative carries its own stored `clips`. The active alternative's stored copy is only refreshed when the user switches or creates an alternative; between those moments the live clips are `track.clips`, and the stored copy goes stale with every main-row edit. Readers that mean "what's in this alternative now" read the stale copy: the render model (lane drawing and hit testing), duplicateTrack, the Inspector badge, getProjectContext (alternativeClipIds), the production brief's track-removal check, handleRemoveTrack, the glue dependency check, the clip-id census. Others legitimately mean the snapshot: the switch, create, delete and restore handlers, persistence, undo capture.

Agent: Simplest fix: keep the stored copy in sync. Every clip write on a track also writes the same change into the active alternative's stored clips. Then every reader is right without changes.

José: every clip write in the app, doubled, through every handler, forever. and the day someone adds a clip handler without the mirror, we're back here. no. one read rule: the active alternative's contents are track.clips, its stored copy is never read for current contents. readers that mean now go through it. the snapshot handlers keep reading the snapshot.

Agent: Understood: no syncing. A model function getAlternativeClips(track, alternative) returns track.clips for the active alternative and the stored clips otherwise, and getHeldClips(track) returns track.clips plus every inactive alternative's stored clips, never the active one's stored copy.

