Agent: For a MIDI clip, the right fragment's source window restamps the loop origin at the split beat (restampLoopOriginEntry(clip, splitBeat)) and prepareMidiClipSplit rebuilds the fragment from only the rows after the cut, re-based to zero. So the fragment's loop starts over at the cut. For audio, the origin is shifted (shiftLoopOriginEntry), which keeps the phase. It's the cut writing a wrong clip, not the scheduler mis-reading a right one. Mine.

