Agent: How to test:
1. On a synth track, make a 4-beat looping MIDI clip 16 beats long with a note held from 1.5 to 2.5, a note from 3.5 to 4.5 that crosses the loop end, and a 50% chance note at beat 1. Play from beat 8 and listen.
2. Split the clip at beat 6 and play from beat 8 again: every note sounds and holds exactly as before, the seam note still strikes at 8 and 12 with nothing new at 10 or 14, and the chance note hits and misses on the same passes.
3. Undo, redo, save and reopen the project: the clip sounds the same each time.
4. Undo, trim the clip start to 6 instead and repeat: same result.
5. On a fresh copy run Delete Time from beat 2 to 7: what follows the cut plays what used to play from beat 7, five beats earlier.
6. Bounce the split clip and compare it with a bounce of the uncut clip: they match.
7. Repeat on a track with a Yeast rack.
8. Split a non-looping MIDI clip: it behaves as before.

